(# Innovation Abstract) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (The proposed invention is an AI-powered adaptive traffic signal optimization system designed to) Tj
T* (dynamically control traffic signals based on real-time and predicted traffic conditions. Unlike) Tj
T* (conventional traffic signal systems that operate using fixed timing schedules or predefined traffic) Tj
T* (rules, the proposed system continuously analyzes traffic conditions and automatically) Tj
T* (determines optimized signal timings.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (The system collects traffic information from cameras, sensors, connected vehicles, and historical) Tj
T* (traffic datasets. AI-based computer vision and machine learning techniques are used to estimate) Tj
T* (vehicle density, queue length, traffic flow, waiting time, and congestion levels at individual road) Tj
T* (segments and intersections.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (The system further predicts short-term traffic conditions using historical and real-time traffic) Tj
T* (patterns. Based on the predicted traffic state, an optimization mechanism dynamically adjusts) Tj
T* (signal phases, green-light duration, red-light duration, and phase priorities.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (The system can also coordinate multiple interconnected traffic signals rather than optimizing) Tj
T* (each intersection independently. This enables traffic flow to be considered across a larger road) Tj
T* (network and reduces the propagation of congestion between neighboring intersections.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (The proposed invention therefore provides an adaptive traffic management mechanism capable) Tj
T* (of continuously sensing, predicting, optimizing, and modifying traffic signal behavior according to) Tj
T* (changing traffic conditions.) Tj
ET
