(# Problem Statement) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Conventional traffic signal systems generally operate using fixed timing schedules or) Tj
T* (predetermined traffic rules. These systems cannot effectively respond to sudden changes in) Tj
T* (traffic volume, unexpected congestion, accidents, road blockages, weather conditions, or) Tj
T* (variations in traffic demand.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (As a result, vehicles may experience unnecessary waiting time even when one direction has) Tj
T* (significantly higher traffic demand than another. Independent operation of traffic signals can also) Tj
T* (create congestion between adjacent intersections and produce inefficient traffic flow across an) Tj
T* (entire road network.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Existing adaptive systems may respond to current traffic conditions but may not sufficiently) Tj
T* (incorporate short-term traffic prediction and coordinated optimization across multiple) Tj
T* (intersections.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (There is therefore a need for an intelligent traffic management system capable of continuously) Tj
T* (detecting current traffic conditions, predicting near-future traffic states, and dynamically) Tj
T* (optimizing traffic signal timings across interconnected intersections.) Tj
ET
